================================================================================
Operating system packages
================================================================================

All published container images are built on a Linux distribution base and
install additional distribution packages:

  - kaimo_file_server (Host), kaimo_file_server.web (Web) and
    kaimo_file_server.samba_bridge: Microsoft's .NET runtime / ASP.NET Core
    images (mcr.microsoft.com/dotnet/runtime:10.0, aspnet:10.0), which are
    based on Ubuntu 24.04 LTS. The .NET runtime itself is MIT-licensed; its
    license and third-party notices are shipped by Microsoft in
    /usr/share/dotnet/LICENSE.txt and /usr/share/dotnet/ThirdPartyNotices.txt.
    Added packages: libgssapi-krb5-2 (all three), postgresql-client-17 (Host,
    Web; from the PostgreSQL Global Development Group (PGDG) apt repository),
    openssh-client, rsync, smbclient, ca-certificates (Web).
  - kaimo_file_server.samba: Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (ubuntu:24.04), plus the shared
    libraries the self-built Samba and the Kaimo helpers link against, python3,
    jq, wsdd and a few base utilities.
  - kaimo_file_server.samba_pki: Alpine Linux 3.22 (alpine:3.22) plus openssl.

These packages are redistributed unmodified, as built by Ubuntu, PGDG and
Alpine. They are under a variety of licenses. Many are permissive (MIT, BSD,
Apache-2.0, PostgreSQL, OpenLDAP, MPL-2.0, ...); copyleft-licensed packages
include, among others:

  - all Ubuntu-based images: the base system (bash, coreutils, dash,
    diffutils, findutils, grep, sed, tar, util-linux, ... -- GPL-2.0/GPL-3.0;
    the GNU C library and other runtime libraries -- LGPL-2.1+/LGPL-3.0+);
  - Samba PKI (Alpine): BusyBox and apk-tools (GPL-2.0-only);
  - Web: rsync (GPL-3.0+), smbclient and the Samba client libraries
    (GPL-3.0+/LGPL-3.0+), talloc/tdb/tevent (LGPL-3.0+), avahi, dbus and
    libtirpc client libraries (LGPL-2.1+/GPL-2.0+);
  - Host and Web: GNU readline (GPL-3.0+, used by psql), gdbm (GPL-3.0+), perl
    (GPL-1.0+ or Artistic), postgresql-client-common (GPL-2.0+);
  - Samba: acl/libacl (GPL-2.0+/LGPL-2.1+), GNU readline (GPL-3.0+), the Ceph
    and GlusterFS client libraries (LGPL), keyutils (GPL-2.0+/LGPL-2.0+).

None of these packages is linked into the AGPL .NET code; they are separate
programs started as processes or libraries used by such programs.

License texts: every Debian/Ubuntu package keeps its license and copyright
notice in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright inside the image (the Ubuntu base
images strip other documentation but explicitly retain these files). Alpine
records each package's license in the apk database (/lib/apk/db/installed).

Exact versions: every image lists the packages it contains in
/usr/share/doc/kaimo/os-packages.txt, generated during the image build. On
Ubuntu each line names the binary package and version and the SOURCE package
and version it was built from; on Alpine each line names the package, version,
origin (source) package and license. Package versions change whenever an
image is rebuilt, so this file -- not this NOTICE -- is authoritative for a
given image. Reproduce it from a pulled image with, for example:

    docker run --rm --entrypoint cat <image> /usr/share/doc/kaimo/os-packages.txt

Source code: the complete source of every package listed there, at exactly
the listed source version, is available from the distributions' permanent
archives:

  - Ubuntu: https://launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/<source-package>/<version>
    (all published versions, including superseded ones), or
    https://snapshot.ubuntu.com/, or "apt-get source <source-package>=<version>"
    on Ubuntu 24.04 with deb-src entries enabled;
  - PGDG (versions containing "pgdg"): https://apt-archive.postgresql.org/
    (permanent archive of all versions published on apt.postgresql.org);
  - Alpine: the build recipes in https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports
    (branch 3.22-stable) and the upstream sources mirrored at
    https://distfiles.alpinelinux.org/distfiles/v3.22/.

